UPDATE companies SET description='Accumold operates from a 15-acre campus in Ankeny, Iowa, just north of Des Moines. The company traces its roots to a rented garage where its founders recognized a growing demand for micro injection molded components that exceeded the capabilities of conventional molding systems. While the exact founding year is not publicly stated, the firm notes four decades of exclusive focus on micro molding and tooling.

Accumold provides vertically integrated micro manufacturing, encompassing tooling, injection molding, micro 3D printing, packaging, and metrology under one roof. Its core process is high-precision thermoplastic injection molding for parts with micron-level tolerances, complemented by additive manufacturing for rapid prototyping. The campus houses advanced metrology including a Zygo NewView 8300 optical profiler, OGP multi-sensor systems, and Keyence vision inspection, enabling measurement of features down to tenths of a micron. The company also offers design for micro molding (DfMM), process validation, and Gage R&R studies.

Materials range from medical-grade biocompatible resins (ISO 10993) to engineering thermoplastics such as ABS, PVC, PMMA, and nylon equivalents.

Accumold differentiates itself by embedding metrology into every production stage, asserting that "if you cannot measure it, you cannot make it." Its vertically integrated model ensures that tooling, molding, and inspection are co-located, allowing rapid iteration and consistent quality at micro scale. The firm emphasizes continuous investment in measurement technology and automation to maintain precision as parts shrink further.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Micro injection molding", "Micro tooling design and fabrication", "Micro 3D printing (additive manufacturing)", "Optical metrology (white light interferometry)", "Multi-sensor dimensional inspection", "Automated vision inspection (AVI)", "Process validation and Gage R&R", "Design for micro molding (DfMM) / Design for manufacturability (DFM)", "Medical micro molding", "Micro-optics molding", "Micro-electronics molding", "Packaging and assembly", "Material selection for micro molding"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Micro-electronics", "Polymer optics", "Automotive electronics", "Emerging technology (wearables, smart devices)"], "materials": ["Medical-grade biocompatible resins (ISO 10993)", "Thermoplastic resins", "ABS-like photopolymers", "PVC-like photopolymers", "PMMA-like photopolymers", "Nylon-like photopolymers"], "equipment": ["Zygo NewView 8300 Optical Profiler", "Optical Gaging Products (OGP) multi-sensor measurement system", "Keyence vision measurement systems with pattern recognition", "Zone3 metrology software", "Automated vision inspection (AVI) systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "Micron-level tolerances, down to tenths of a micron", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated tooling, molding, packaging, and metrology on a single 15-acre campus", "Sub-nanometer optical metrology (Zygo NewView 8300) and multi-sensor measurement systems", "Measurement development and Gage R&R integrated from the design phase", "Micro 3D printing for precision prototypes and production bridging", "Four decades dedicated exclusively to micro molding and tooling"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Ankeny, Iowa -> db, /about-us", "Founded in rented garage -> /about-us", "40 years dedicated to micro molding and tooling -> /", "Vertically integrated tooling, molding, packaging, metrology on 15-acre campus -> /about-us", "Markets: Medical, Micro Electronics, Polymer Optics, Emerging Tech, Automotive Electronics -> /", "Micro molding process description -> /", "Metrology equipment: Zygo NewView 8300, OGP multi-sensor, Keyence, Zone3 software -> /quality", "Gage R&R, DFM/DfMM -> /quality", "Automated vision inspection (AVI) -> /quality", "Materials: medical-grade biocompatible (ISO 10993), ABS-like, PVC-like, PMMA-like, Nylon-like -> /, industries_served", "Tolerances: micron, half-micron, tenths of micron -> /quality, /", "Micro 3D printing services -> /", "Company type evidence -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "All tooling, molding, packaging, and metrology processes are completed on our 15-acre campus near Des Moines, Iowa", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='accumold' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Accusemble Electronics Inc. was founded in 1979 and operates from North Billerica, Massachusetts. The company is led by President Deborah Bayley and has built its reputation on the principles of quality, value, and service.

The company provides custom circuit board assembly and contract manufacturing services ranging from engineering prototypes and new product introduction (NPI) through low-, medium-, and high-volume production runs. Its capabilities include surface-mount technology (SMT) assembly using five Yamaha pick-and-place systems, automated optical and X-ray inspection, drag soldering and hybrid heating rework stations, conformal coating with urethane and acrylic materials, and full supply-chain procurement. The facility also offers extensive rework and repair services for electronic assemblies.

Accusemble serves both defense and commercial markets. In the defense sector it delivers mission-critical circuit board assemblies built to rigorous standards. Commercial customers span consumer electronics and industrial applications, where the company supplies custom, high-quality circuit board solutions.

The business was started to provide high-quality contract manufacturing with a focus on continual improvement of manufacturing methods. President Deborah Bayley states that the company maintains a constant desire to offer products and services of superior quality and workmanship, supported by an in-house IPC-A-610-certified trainer and advanced inspection technology.', certifications=ARRAY['IPC-A-610']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom circuit board assembly (IPC Class 1, 2, 3)", "Engineering prototype & new product introduction (NPI)", "Low-, medium-, and high-volume production assembly", "Rework and repair of electronic assemblies", "Full engineering support", "SMT assembly with Yamaha pick-and-place systems", "Automated optical inspection (AOI) and X-ray inspection", "Automated soldering (drag soldering, hybrid heating rework)", "Conformal coating (urethane, acrylic)", "Supply chain management and procurement"], "industries": ["Defense", "Commercial", "Consumer electronics", "Industrial applications"], "materials": ["Urethane conformal coating", "Acrylic conformal coating"], "equipment": ["5 Yamaha SMT pick-and-place systems", "Yamaha Ysi-V AOI system", "X-ray inspection system", "Drag soldering stations", "Hybrid heating rework stations"], "volume": "Prototype to high volume production runs", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Specialization in IPC Class 3 assembly", "In-house IPC-A-610 certified trainer", "Five Yamaha SMT pick-and-place systems for ultra-high-speed placement", "Yamaha Ysi-V AOI and X-ray inspection for hidden defects", "Comprehensive rework and repair services"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1979 -> /about-us", "Headquarters in North Billerica, Massachusetts -> /about-us, /", "President Deborah Bayley -> /about-us", "Principles: Quality, Value, Service -> /about-us, /", "Custom circuit board assembly Class 1,2,3 specialization in Class 3 -> /, /services, /capabilities", "Engineering prototype & NPI -> /, /services, /capabilities", "Low-medium-high volume assembly -> /, /services, /capabilities", "Rework/repair capabilities -> /, /services, /capabilities", "Full engineering support -> /services", "SMT assembly with 5 Yamaha PNP systems -> /capabilities", "Yamaha Ysi-V AOI and X-ray inspection -> /capabilities", "Drag soldering & hybrid heating rework stations -> /capabilities", "Conformal coating urethane and acrylic -> /capabilities", "Supply chain & procurement -> /capabilities", "IPC-A-610-certified trainer in-house -> /capabilities", "Industries served: Defense and Commercial (consumer electronics, industrial) -> /, /capabilities", "Volume: prototype pieces to high volume production runs -> /about-us", "Company type: contract manufacturer -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Accusemble Electronics is committed to providing our customers with high quality contract manufacturing services and related products.", "founded_year": "1979", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='accusemble-electronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Accutech Fabrication Inc operates from Lynchburg, Virginia. The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed in the available sources. It presents itself as a sheet metal fabrication and machining shop serving a range of industrial customers.

The shop provides sheet metal fabrication and CNC machining services. Its capabilities include press brake bending, laser cutting, multi-axis milling, powder coating, rolling, sandblasting, MIG and TIG welding, and band saw cutting. Equipment listed includes a Proto Trak3 2-axis CNC mill with 32 inches of travel and a Track DPM RX5 CNC bed mill with a 30 by 15 inch table and 40 inches of travel. Part size capacity ranges up to 144 by 144 inches for brake work, 59 by 119 inches for laser cutting, and 90 by 90 by 240 inches for machining, with a 60-inch width capacity for unlimited length on certain operations. The company states it handles projects from prototyping through production runs.

The company serves industrial manufacturing, automotive, and electronics sectors. Its brake forming services are described as suitable for creating precise and complex parts across many industries.

