UPDATE companies SET description='Advanced Circuitry International was founded in 1992 in Duluth, Georgia, as an independently owned manufacturer of high-reliability RF/microwave and antenna printed circuit boards. The company began with a focus on aerospace, defense, telecommunications, and medical device markets, building expertise in exotic substrates such as Teflon and ceramics.

Today the company operates a 70,000-square-foot facility and is expanding into an additional 50,000 square feet. Its capabilities span RF/microwave PCBs, antenna PCBs, large-format boards up to 24 by 102 inches, multilayer constructions, rapid prototyping, and full assembly of RF/microwave and antenna sub-systems. The shop also provides design-for-manufacturability assistance, impedance modeling, in-process and final inspection testing, and a logistics program that stocks laminate materials and finished goods for qualified customers.

Advanced Circuitry serves a global base of OEMs and EMS providers across land, sea, air, and space applications. Specific markets include 5G infrastructure, base stations, GPS, microwave communications, small cells, automotive electronics, and marine systems. The company''s customer list includes notable original equipment manufacturers and electronics manufacturing services firms worldwide.

It emphasizes control of passive intermodulation (PIM) for low-PIM applications, rapid turnaround supported by a large inventory of RF materials, and the ability to produce exceptionally large antenna structures on a wide range of high-frequency laminates.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100D','ISO 9001:2015','ITAR registered','RoHS compliant','REACH compliant','IPC-6011','IPC-6012','IPC-6018','IPC-A-600','IPC-610','J-STD-001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["RF/microwave PCB fabrication", "Antenna PCB fabrication", "Large-format PCB fabrication (up to 24\u2033 \u00d7 102\u2033)", "Multilayer PCB fabrication", "Rapid prototyping", "RF/microwave and antenna PCB assembly", "Design for manufacturability (DFM) assistance", "Impedance modeling and verification", "In-process and final inspection testing", "Logistics and material stocking program"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Telecommunications", "Medical devices", "5G infrastructure", "Base station", "GPS", "Microwave communications", "Small cell", "Automotive", "Marine"], "materials": ["PTFE (Teflon)", "Ceramics", "Epoxies", "High-speed low-loss laminates", "RF/microwave substrates"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to large-scale production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Large-format PCB capability up to 24\u2033 \u00d7 102\u2033", "Rapid prototyping backed by extensive RF material stock", "ITAR registered for defense-related work", "Low-PIM process control for high-reliability RF applications"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1992 in Duluth, GA -> /about-us", "Independently owned -> /about-us", "70,000 sqft facility, expanding 50,000 sqft -> /about-us, / (New State-of-the-Art Facility)", "Manufactures RF/microwave, antenna, large-format, multilayer PCBs -> /, /capabilities", "Rapid prototyping with stocked RF materials -> / (RAPID PROTOTYPING)", "Large format up to 24\" x 102\" -> / (LARGE FORMAT PCB''S)", "Assembly of RF/microwave and antenna sub-systems -> / (RF/MICROWAVE & ANTENNA PCB