UPDATE companies SET description='AdvancedPCB is an American-based printed circuit board manufacturer headquartered in Maple Grove, Minnesota. The company operates domestic manufacturing facilities and provides engineering oversight for both prototype and volume production.

AdvancedPCB offers a full spectrum of PCB services, including fabrication of standard (0-10 layer), advanced (up to 40 layers), HDI, rigid-flex (4-22 layers), and heavy copper boards, as well as quick-turn prototypes with turnaround as fast as 24 hours. Its assembly division handles SMT, through-hole, and mixed-technology builds with turnkey, partial turnkey, or consigned parts options and no minimum order quantity. The company also provides design services for high-speed digital, RF, and HDI circuits, DFM reviews, and global manufacturing through certified offshore partners with U.S. engineering oversight.

The company serves aerospace and defense, telecommunications and networking, data centers and cloud computing, industrial and robotics, medical devices, automotive, consumer electronics, and computing/AI hardware sectors. Customers range from defense primes requiring AS9100 and ITAR compliance to commercial OEMs scaling from prototype to high-volume production.

AdvancedPCB emphasizes its integrated domestic fabrication and assembly under one roof to reduce handoff risk, military-grade security with ITAR-compliant data handling, and a ''Made in America'' model that ships worldwide. The firm also highlights rapid prototyping offers such as same-day turns and weekend delivery programs to accelerate R&D cycles.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100','ITAR','ROHS','ISO9001','CMMC']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB fabrication (0-40 layers)", "HDI and UHDI PCBs", "Rigid-flex circuits (4-22 layers)", "Heavy copper PCBs", "Quick-turn prototypes (24-hour turnaround)", "Standard PCBs (0-10 layers)", "Flex circuits (1-6 layers)", "PCB assembly (SMT, thru-hole, mixed technology)", "Turnkey/partial turnkey/consignment assembly", "Design services (high-speed digital, RF, rigid-flex, HDI)", "DFM services", "Global manufacturing with U.S. engineering oversight", "Conformal coating, potting, encapsulation", "IPC Class 2/Class 3 compliance", "AS9100 quality standards", "ITAR compliance", "RoHS compliant processes", "Lead-free and leaded solder", "Impedance calculation", "Panel utilization and array drawings", "Vendor-managed inventory (VMI) programs"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Defense", "Telecommunications", "Data Centers and Networking", "Industrial and Robotics", "Medical Devices", "Automotive", "Consumer Electronics", "Computing and AI Hardware"], "materials": ["FR-4", "RF materials", "Aluminum clad", "Heavy copper", "Custom materials"], "equipment": ["Strip-Etch-Strip line"], "volume": "Prototype to high volume (1 to 1000+ units for standard PCBs; no minimum for assembly)", "lead_time": "As fast as 24 hours for prototypes; same-day to 4 weeks depending on complexity", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Integrated domestic PCB fabrication and assembly under one roof", "Manufacturing turn times as fast as 24 hours for prototypes", "No minimum order quantity for assembly services", "ITAR-compliant data submission and military-grade securi