UPDATE companies SET description='Ahner Industrial Fabricating & Sheet Metal operates a 45,000-square-foot fabrication facility in Sandusky, Ohio. The family-owned shop traces its roots to the Ahner Sheet Metal business that has been part of the Sandusky industrial landscape for decades, though a specific founding year is not publicly stated. Today the company runs cutting, forming, welding, and assembly under one roof, supported by 2- to 5-ton overhead cranes and multiple jib cranes for handling large weldments and structural assemblies.

The shop focuses on short-run and repeat production of metal components, from laser-cut and formed brackets to full industrial ductwork packages and large welded frames for equipment such as heater houses. Capabilities span laser cutting, press-brake forming, MIG/TIG welding, finishing, hardware installation, and final assembly. Work can start from a complete CAD model, a 2D drawing, a photograph, a hand sketch, or an existing sample part that needs replication.

Ahner serves a broad industrial base including automotive, electronics, air handling, material handling, lighting, food processing, industrial machinery, amusement parks, steel and foundry operations, construction, general manufacturing, injection molding, chemical, marine, containers, oil and energy, and quarry operations.

The company emphasizes a single-point-of-contact approach: customers work directly with the fabrication team to define process scope, critical fits, material selection, inspection requirements, and delivery logistics before any work is committed. An online Price CAD tool supports instant quoting for production-ready sheet metal parts, while custom requests move through a structured review of manufacturability and timing.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Laser cutting", "Forming (press brake)", "Welding (MIG/TIG)", "Finishing", "Assembly", "Short-run fabrication", "Replacement part fabrication", "Repeat production", "Weldment fabrication", "Industrial ductwork fabrication", "Large welded assembly fabrication", "Stainless steel fabrication", "Carbon steel fabrication"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Electronics", "Air Handling", "Material Handling", "Lighting", "Food Processing", "Industrial Machinery", "Amusement Parks", "Steel & Foundry", "Construction", "General Manufacturing", "Injection Molding", "Chemical", "Marine", "Containers", "Oil & Energy", "Quarries"], "materials": ["Stainless steel", "Carbon steel"], "equipment": ["2-5 ton overhead cranes", "jib cranes"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned, 45,000 sq ft facility with overhead crane capacity up to 5 tons", "Accepts CAD, drawings, photos, sketches, or physical samples to start a quote", "In-house laser cutting, forming, welding, finishing, and assembly under one roof", "Price CAD Online for instant quoting on production-ready sheet metal parts", "Handles short runs, replacement parts, and repeat production volumes"], "facts_used": ["Family-owned fabrication shop in Sandusky, Ohio -> /about", "45,000-square-foot facility -> /about", "2-5 ton overhead cranes and jib cranes -> db (description)", "Laser cutting, forming, welding, finishing, assembly -> /", "Short runs, replacement parts, repeat production -> /", "Accepts CAD, drawings, photos, sketches, samples -> /", "Price CAD Online for production-ready sheet metal parts -> /", "Industries served list (17 industries) -> /about", "Stainless steel and carbon steel examples -> /", "Single-point-of-contact approach, structured review -> /about", "No founding year explicitly stated -> /about", "No employee count stated -> /about", "No certifications stated -> /about", "No volume range, lead time, tolerances stated -> /", "No CAGE code, min order, export compliance, languages, social links -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Ahner Industrial is a family-owned fabrication shop in Sandusky, Ohio. We help customers turn drawings, existing parts, and practical manufacturing needs into fabricated components and assemblies.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ahner-industrial-fabricating-sheet-metal' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Airslamit operates from Gilbert, Arizona, as an online retailer specializing in air ride suspension systems for classic cars and trucks. The founding year and ownership structure are not disclosed in public materials; the storefront is staffed by personnel including a team member named Thomas who assists customers with product selection.

The company curates and sells complete air ride kits and individual components from multiple brands, including airmaxxx, Air Lift, Slam Specialties, and AccuAir. Its catalog covers vehicle-specific kits for platforms such as 1958–2018 Chevrolet C10, Silverado, Impala, and Cadillac models; 1964–1996 GM A-, B-, and G-body cars; Buick and Riviera models; and import mini trucks. Offerings range from air springs and management systems (including AccuAir Endo-VT packages) to compressors, valves, wiring kits, and mounting hardware. Some mounting plates are noted as made in the USA.

