UPDATE companies SET description='Alabama Chanin operates from Florence, Alabama, where it began in 2000 with a documentary film titled Stitch and 200 hand-crafted T-shirts made by artisans in the Shoals region. The organization formally established as Alabama Chanin in 2006 and now functions as a 501(c)(3) nonprofit under Project Threadways, a single not-for-profit entity that also encompasses The School of Making and arts and humanities programs.

The company designs and produces textiles by hand, specializing in artisan-led clothing and made-to-order pieces crafted from organic cotton fabrics using slow, intentional methods. A new headquarters and community space, The Maker Lab broke ground in January 2026 to house studios, workshop rooms, exhibitions, a café, and retail. The organization also publishes books, kits, and patterns, and runs workshops teaching sewing, embroidery, and design exploration for over 100 participants per session.

Alabama Chanin serves direct consumers purchasing high-end garments (priced from $698 to $2,858), craft-education participants, and attendees of its Project Threadways symposiums on sustainability and textile culture. Past collaborations include a long-standing partnership with Heath Ceramics beginning in 2011, and a pandemic pivot to producing face masks in 2020. Its archive preserves two decades of oral histories, oral history interviews, and public history projects.

The enterprise was founded on the belief that making holds power—emphasizing transparent supply chains, ethical labor, cultural heritage preservation, and creative placemaking. Its mission integrates production, education, and documentation to sustain artisan craft and keep continuity between makers, materials, and place.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Hand-sewing", "Hand-crafted textile production", "Slow design methodology", "Artisan-led garment assembly", "Organic cotton fabric sourcing", "Pattern making", "Fabric painting", "Embroidery", "Craft skill workshops", "Oral history documentation", "Archive management", "Symposium and event organization", "Community space management", "Made-to-order garment production", "Retail operations"], "industries": ["Fashion and apparel", "Textile manufacturing", "Craft education", "Cultural heritage preservation", "Arts and humanities", "Community development", "Nonprofit arts organizations"], "materials": ["Organic cotton"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Hand-sewn production in Florence, Alabama", "Slow design and artisan-led manufacturing", "Transparent supply chains and ethical labor practices", "Organic cotton materials", "Integrated craft education, archive, and community programs"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2006 -> /", "Headquarters Florence, Alabama -> /", "Nonprofit 501(c)(3) status -> /", "Hand-sewn organic cotton clothing production -> /", "School of Making workshops -> /", "Arts and humanities archive and symposiums -> /", "Maker Lab new headquarters ground broken January 2026 -> /", "Heath Ceramics collaboration since 2011 -> /", "COVID-19 face mask production 2020 -> /", "Organic cotton materials -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We design and produce textiles by hand.", "founded_year": "2006", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [