UPDATE companies SET description='Alpha Custom Apparel operates from West Bend, Wisconsin. The company was founded by Christina Ongert, who serves as president and owner, drawing on 27 years of fashion and manufacturing experience. Ongert established the business to assist independent fashion brands, organizations, companies, and e‑commerce retailers with sourcing, textile production, and broader manufacturing needs.

The firm manages the full supply chain — design and development, fabric and trim sourcing, sample creation, bulk production, packaging, quality‑control checks, and delivery logistics. It leverages a global network of manufacturing partners while emphasizing localized decoration and production to reduce costs, emissions, and lead times. Product categories span athletic and team apparel, promotional and hardline items, retail and corporate apparel, construction‑grade hi‑vis gear, and managed company stores.

Clients range from independent fashion labels and online retailers to schools, nonprofits, and corporate brands. Notable partnerships include Good Karma Brands and the ESPN Tailgate at the Tundra Trio in Green Bay, where Alpha supplies branded giveaways such as hats, blankets, and fans. The company also supports local organizations like West Bend High Schools, the Wisconsin 911 Memorial, and various community nonprofits.

Alpha differentiates itself through an innovative design approach and a stated goal of cutting concept‑to‑completion time in half. The leadership team positions the company as a creative partner that brings fashion‑forward thinking to industries that traditionally treat apparel as purely functional, aiming to empower anyone with a creative idea to launch or grow a brand.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom apparel design and development", "Fabric and trim sourcing", "Sample production", "Bulk production management", "Packaging and quality control", "Logistics and delivery coordination", "Localized decoration and manufacturing", "Global manufacturing network management", "Promotional product sourcing and branding", "Company store setup and management", "Athletic and team apparel production", "Corporate apparel programs", "Construction hi\u2011vis apparel programs", "Customized service (tailored product selection)", "Speed\u2011to\u2011market supply chain optimization"], "industries": ["Independent fashion brands", "E-commerce retailers", "Corporate branding", "Sports and athletics", "Education (schools)", "Nonprofit organizations", "Construction (hi-vis apparel)", "Promotional products", "Retail apparel"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Innovative design approach combined with speed\u2011to\u2011market focus", "Localized decoration and manufacturing to lower costs and emissions", "Global manufacturing network for competitive, sustainable production", "Customized service that curates tailored options instead of catalog browsing", "Streamlined supply chain aiming to halve concept\u2011to\u2011completion time"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in West Bend, Wisconsin -> db", "Founded by Christina Ongert, President + Owner -> /about-us", "Christina Ongert has 27 years experience in fashion and manufacturing -> /about-us", "Company handles full supply chain: design, sourcing, samples, bulk production, packaging, quality control, delivery -> /about-us", "Partners with global manufacturers, emphasizes localized decoration and manufacturing -> /about-us", "Product categories: athletic/team apparel, promotional/hardline items, retail apparel, corporate apparel, construction/hi-vis, company stores -> /", "Serves independent fashion brands, organizations, companies, e-commerce retailers -> /about-us", "Partnership with Good Karma Brands and ESPN Tailgate at Tundra Trio -> /", "Community sponsorships: West Bend High Schools, Wisconsin 911 Memorial, West Bend Power Hockey, etc. -> /", "Differentiators: innovative design approach, speed to market, customized service, global network, localized production -> / and /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "CLOTHING MANUFACTURER AND PROMOTIONAL DECORATOR", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='alpha-custom-apparel' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Alpha Electric Supply was founded in 1987 on the island of Maui by four electrical-supply veterans with a combined 105 years of experience. The company is headquartered in Honolulu, Hawaii, and is owned by Honsador Holdings LLC and Doman Building Materials Group Ltd. Honsador, a Hawaiian business dating back to 1935, operates 15 branch locations across the islands and employs over 250 people across its family of companies.

Alpha operates as a wholesale distributor of electrical products, sourcing from a broad network of manufacturers rather than producing its own goods. Its branches on Maui, Oahu, Kauai, and the Big Island (Hilo and Kona) stock wire, conduit, lighting, circuit breakers, switchgear, photovoltaic equipment, and related materials. The company provides delivery using a fleet of vans, pickup trucks, stakebed/flatbed trucks, and heavy-duty utility trucks, and offers project pricing, credit accounts with Net 30 terms, and takeoff/quotation services from customer plans.

The supplier serves commercial, industrial, residential, utility, and photovoltaic market segments throughout Hawaii. Alpha also supports commercial energy projects and home energy solutions through dedicated programs.

The company’s stated differentiator is a service philosophy captured in its motto: the customer is the purpose of the business, not an interruption. Alpha emphasizes that it does not private-label products, maintains market-specific inventory from qualified manufacturers, and leverages long-standing vendor relationships to secure competitive pricing and availability.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Delivery services (jobsite and shop)", "Project pricing and bidding", "Credit account management (Net 30, authorized signers)", "Inventory management and stocking", "Takeoffs and quotations from plans", "Lighting and apparatus bid process", "Rough-in material quoting", "Vendor sourcing and procurement"], "industries": ["Commercial Energy & Project Solutions", "Home Energy & Safety Solutions", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Residential", "Utility", "Photovoltaic", "Building Materials"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Vans", "Pickup trucks", "Stakebed/flatbed trucks", "Heavy-duty utility trucks"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No private-label products; all stock from qualified manufacturers", "Delivery fleet including vans, pickups, stakebed/flatbed and heavy-duty utility trucks", "Project pricing and lighting/apparatus bid process for jobs of any size", "Credit accounts with Net 30 terms and authorized-signer controls", "Takeoff and quotation services from customer plans"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1987 in Hawaii by four leaders with 105 years combined experience -> /about-us", "Owned by Honsador Holdings LLC and Doman Building Materials Group Ltd. -> /about-us", "Honsador founded 1935, 15 branch locations, over 250 employees across group -> /about-us", "Branches on Maui, Oahu, Kauai, Big Island (Hilo, Kona) -> /about-us", "Serves commercial, industrial, residential, utility, photovoltaic markets -> /about-us", "Delivery fleet: vans, pickup trucks, stakebed/flatbed trucks, heavy-duty utility trucks -> /services", "Project pricing and lighting/apparatus bid process -> /services", "Credit accounts with Net 30 terms and authorized signers -> /services", "Inventory from qualified manufacturers, no private labeling -> /services", "Takeoffs and quotations from customer plans -> /services", "Headquarters in Honolulu, Hawaii -> db", "Industries served: Commercial Energy & Project Solutions, Home Energy & Safety Solutions -> db"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Alpha Electric Supply is able to obtain products from a wide variety of vendors.", "founded_year": "1987", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='alpha-electric-supply' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Alpha Plastics, Inc. operates from Coon Rapids, Minnesota, where it was founded in 1976. The company is family- and veteran-owned, drawing on over 100 years of combined experience among its team.

The shop specializes in plastic pressure forming and thermoforming, producing parts such as polycarbonate defrosting ducts, polyethylene shrouds and dump wagon tubs, polycarbonate access doors, and Kydex shrouds. It runs prototype, short-run, and long-run production, and offers value-added services including assembly, finishing, custom packaging, logistics support, and EMI coatings.

Alpha Plastics serves customers across the United States and ships to Mexico.

